one of the latest additions to escape  from tarkov  might be one of my favorites yet scav  karma  for me scavs have always been integral  to the game both in terms of gameplay  but also the core target of experience  and  as accessibility to newer players and  now the whole element of playing as a  scavenger through the lands of tarkov is  more fun  more experiential and most importantly  more profitable  i've always considered scavens to be the  great equalizer in tarkov nothing  ventured  everything gained the start of every  underdog story that begins with a cheeky  breaky reserve run and snowballs into  piles of rubles and a stash fill to the  brim  in a game that's quickly occupied by the  juiciest of pmcs just days after the  wipe scavrons allow the more casual less  experienced or financially challenged  players a leg up against the snowballing  armored menaces now for those players  that may rely on said scaverns and have  missed the moving and shaking of tarkov  these recent weeks what is scav karma  and how does it work  you can view your karma by looking at  your fence reputation and can be earned  in a few very easy ways firstly it's all  about that sweet sweet cooperation so  using the cob extracts as either scav or  pmc  using car extracts as either of your  characters or my personal favorite way  to gain that sweet sweet karma  revenge  killing a pmc or any scav that has done  harm to your fellow scavengers will  improve how fence and in relation  how ai scavs feel about you but what  does all this wholesome bloodshed get  you  well players with a higher reputation  with fence will spawn into their  scavenge with much better gear  more valuable loot and find the ai scavs  in the game are much friendlier to you  than they are to those who commit the  cardinal sin of scav on scout violence  in addition if you reach the very peak  of scav karma then fence will sell you  leftover  uninsured pmc gear from deceased players  most importantly though i feel that scav  karma incentives cooperation  as you are directly contributing to  stopping scavs turning on each other  and actively working together or at the  very least shifting watching over your  backs as you cautiously move to extract  as a rag tag  untrusting group waiting to be picked  off by an opportune sniper  overall i feel like this has really  helped develop the overall game to game  raid to raid vibe and experience of  escape from tarkov classically it's  always been somewhat  free-for-all regardless of what faction  you're playing as but i always felt that  it's more fitting that scavs band  together and work with whatever cursed  ak they've been unfortunate to spawn  with  against the more highly geared pmcs the  common people rising up against the  rich and the well-armed that isn't to  say that tarkov still isn't the brutal  place we all know and love  regardless of how much kindness you show  your fellow scav in the time  i've been playing since the addition of  karma i felt both hope  and the sting of betrayal i've been left  cautiously waiting at co-op extracts  only for a kind pair of scavs to pick me  up  and welcome me along to the rest of  their journey constantly watching over  their shoulder to ensure that the  stranger with a rifle that follows the  back of the pack  doesn't turn on them i've also been far  too trusting as well  signaling scavs to join me waiting for  them extract seeing them do the classic  friendly wriggle  only for them to launch a supersonic  piece of metal through my cerebellum  so that it could loot my carton of uht  milk natural cooperation was always  rare in tarkov and while it can still be  hard to come by it's  way more commonplace now that players  are getting to grips with the ups and  downs of karma  for me i always felt that this  cooperation should have been encouraged  more  tarkov is a rough place to hang out and  whether teaming up was planned before  the raid or found halfway through it  it's always beneficial to be involved  well  usually but because the idea of teamwork  and tarkov  is a fairly new concept whenever it  happens it feels all that more impactful  the scav i teamed up with was nameless  i'll never know who they were  but they watched my back as i looted  held angles for me while i healed  provided me with a beam of light when it  was dark and helped me when i was  wounded  it was a fleeting bond created on a whim  in the battlefield  with a total stranger but damn it when i  saw that pmc drop him i felt  furious he was my friend my nameless  strange filthy friend the smart play  would have been to shrug it off  as doggy dog it's ruthless out there  especially when that pmc was much more  well geared than i was  but i felt i owed it to my fallen  comrade to at least  try to avenge them  it wasn't an experience i expected to  have especially as in my hundreds of  hours in tarkov it's  mostly been a solo isolated and honestly  sometimes lonely experience  but seeing scavs that are real players  team up and create these little moments  of cooperation  i think really enriches the tarkov  experience  for any kind of player for me at least  they're interesting and unique enough  that the events  are worth more to me than the loot i  leave with or any rewards i might  receive from fence  that is unless i spawn with a labs card  in that case you'll get out of my face  and you get out of my way  now not everyone is fully sold on the  new karma system and plenty of  disheveled survivors are still  as greedy and bloodthirsty as ever that  is to be expected as we are all  still human and as such fall to human  emotions  i can't say i wouldn't be tempted to  pull a trigger if i knew my scav friend  i met in reserve had a gpu in their  backpack  but that makes the whole concept all  that more deep and  interesting both in a gameplay sense  lore sense and experiential sense  i think that this in the grand scheme of  things small change to escape from  tarkov  has done a lot to help much of the game  grow i think new players will feel more  welcome  and find accomplishments within it while  veteran players are able to make new  experiences  within the game as well and hopefully it  helps all of us go home just  a few rubles richer  in the process of making expert react  this week i have been playing a bunch  more tarkov  but this was something that just stuck  in my brain and i wanted to share my  thoughts with you all  so with that said i hope you enjoyed the  video let me know your thoughts about it  all in the comment section below  subscribe for more and as always i'll  see you next time  [Music]  you

